    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the bit about anecdotal vs empirical, but it feels deeper than just being 'exceptional.' it's not just that i'm good at things, it's the metabolic efficiency of it all. like, my brain doesn't seem to have the same 'overhead' or fatigue spikes that others do. if we look past the standard medical definitions, are there any theoretical frameworks for what might be considered a biological optimization or a shift toward a more high-frequency human baseline?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
