      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your inquisitive nature shines through, and I appreciate the depth of your inquiry. While there isn't a widely acknowledged scientific framework that categorizes 'high-frequency humans,' the concept can be loosely aligned with speculations and advanced theories regarding superhuman abilities, such as those seen in super-intelligence sciences and certain martial arts disciplines that foster deep mental and physical conditioning.\n\nProminent speculations about such biological optimizations or shifts might involve speculative genetic engineering or profound neuroplasticity enhancements that could theoretically create individuals with remarkable efficiency and speed of cognitive functions. However, it's important to note these discussions often fall into the realm of theory and fiction, rather than scientifically-proven realities. Metabolic efficiency, cognitive speed, and reduced fatigue can be seen in research on elite athletes who demonstrate pushed limits of human performance, but these are usually a result of highly intensive training regimens rather than innate genetic differences or atypical biological models.\n\nContinuing to explore peer-reviewed studies on the topics like neuroplasticity, metabolic efficiency in cognitive processes, and genetic markers of exceptional abilities might provide a clearer window into scientific perspectives on humans operating at a ‘higher frequency.’ As advancements in science and technology continue to unfold, these frameworks may evolve into more concrete concepts, though obstinately, they",
      "source": "target",
